{#
  Canonical icon block — the site's favicon / touch-icon set.

  SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH. Included once from base.njk's <head>, before
  {{ head_extras }}, so every page gets the identical set with no per-page
  edit. Extracted 2026-08-29 from the 52 per-page `-head.html` files that each
  carried their own copy — 256 duplicated <link> lines across 54 files.

  The extraction fixed three defects by construction rather than by hand:
    • /bitcoin-fixed-income   — had NO icon block at all
    • /bitcoin-vs-real-estate — had NO icon block at all
    • /the-melting-ice-cube   — carried only the SVG line; missing the .ico,
                                both PNG sizes and the apple-touch-icon

  Kin to the `canonical-nav-css` and `canonical-ribbon-css` blocks in base.njk:
  site chrome belongs to the layout, not to 54 copies of itself.

  ── ORDER MATTERS ──
  The SVG is declared first on purpose. Browsers that support SVG favicons
  prefer the first supported declaration, so the vector wins on modern
  desktop; the .ico and PNGs are the ladder down for everything else, and
  Safari takes the apple-touch-icon. A consequence worth stating because it
  is easy to get wrong: swapping only the PNGs and leaving the SVG stale
  would leave most desktop users looking at the OLD mark. The whole set is
  replaced together or not at all.

  ── PROVENANCE ──
  The raster set is generated from the brand mark and lives in `brand/`
  (see SITE_GUIDE). Files are served from the site root and registered in
  `.eleventy.js` staticAssets. `favicon-192x192.png` is deliberately NOT
  linked here — it is retained at root for any future web-app manifest and
  has never been part of the <head> set.
#}
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico">
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="48x48" href="/favicon-48x48.png">
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32x32.png">
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16x16.png">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
